{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For therefore, etc.</b> That is, so they should not say: How does he invite them to eat after he recognized them to be ministers of the Most High? For although we explained that he intended in his words to allude to spirituality, even so the plain sense is not uprooted, and in the food too there are wondrous secrets, as stated (Proverbs 13:25): ״צַדִּיק אוֹכֵל לְשׂוֹבַע נַפְשׁוֹ״ — within the inwardness of spirituality. Therefore he said to them <b>for</b>, etc. — meaning, there is a reason for my words: <b>therefore have you passed by</b>, meaning, in this order, in the likeness of men — for there also exists [sustenance] in physical food. <b>And they said: So do</b> — meaning, yes, it is as his words: that therefore they had passed by him in the likeness of men, and they agreed with him to do as he had spoken. Further, they hinted to him that he should do in the manner expressed in his words — to let them taste the spirituality fitting for them, as alluded to in his words, as I have explained."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:52.832818313Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}